    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0299" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.01/421: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-03-07T11:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7,
                                1925—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 7—10:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>94. The Foreign Office having heard from Sir Esme Howard<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d178-f1"/> that the Palestine mandate treaty<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d178-f2"/> has been ratified by the Senate, asks me by an informal
                    communication whether we are ready to proceed to the exchange of
                    ratifications.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
